messages:
Emily Chen: Heads-up: docsite search results are landing on the canonical page but losing the fragment. Example: search points to /api (redirects) but the #tokenization anchor never gets applied. Seen in prod search results.

Jason Park: Repro'd locally. Clicking a search result that goes through our redirect drops the hash. Looks like server-side redirects can't preserve URL fragments — Docusaurus handles hash scrolling client-side.

Liam O'Connor: Could add a client-side fallback that checks document.referrer for a hash and scrolls to it after redirect. Pretty small JS shim in the theme.

Sophia Reyes: I sketched one:
```js
// theme/js/hash-fallback.js
window.addEventListener('load', () => {
  try {
    const ref = document.referrer && new URL(document.referrer);
    if (ref && ref.hash && !location.hash) {
      // tiny delay to let Docusaurus render sections
      setTimeout(() => window.location.hash = ref.hash, 50);
    }
  } catch (e) { console.warn('hash-fallback fail', e); }
});
```

Emily Chen: Nice. Can you open a PR? ping @docs-oncall when ready. :thumbsup:

Jason Park: Also noticed some builders produce different slugify behaviour — MkDocs slug `tokenization` vs MDX slug `Tokenization`. Broken anchors in linkcheck were throwing warnings: `Broken anchor: Tokenization -> tokenization`. We should add explicit anchors in the markdown too, e.g. `### Tokenization {#tokenization}` to be stable.

Liam O'Connor: Agreed — explicit ids are the most robust across toolchains. Let's do both explicit id and the JS fallback so old external redirects also get something.

Sophia Reyes: PR opened: https://github.com/redwood-inference/docs/pull/4321 — includes theme JS + md fixes. CI failed lint on a code fence spacing issue.

Emily Chen: I'll take the lint fix. Also can we add a smoke test for search->fragment behavior? Prefer a Puppeteer check that simulates clicking a search result and asserts location.hash. Cypress might be heav(ier).

Jason Park: Puppeteer sounds good. Keep it in tests/e2e/search-hash.spec.js and mark as smoke. Avoid flakiness by waiting for networkidle and then checking hash.

Sophia Reyes: Added a Puppeteer test in the PR and it passes locally. CI error was `E302 expected 2 blank lines, found 1` in the MDX file — fixed that and pushed.

Emily Chen: Preview deploy looks good — clicking the search result lands and scrolls to the section. @Liam O'Connor can you review? :eyes:

Liam O'Connor: Reviewing now. Small nit: the setTimeout 50ms could be 100ms to be safer on slow clients. Approved after that tweak.

Sophia Reyes: Updated to 100ms. Tests still pass. Ready to merge.

deploy-bot: Deployment started for branch stable -> prod at 2026-03-21T10:12:03Z

Emily Chen: Thanks! One caveat: external redirects that are configured on old domains and point to /api without a hash will still lose fragment unless the original link included the hash in the referer. Filed follow-up issue: https://github.com/redwood-inference/docs/issues/789 about adding CDN-level redirect hinting to attach fragments when possible. @Jason Park please triage with infra.

Jason Park: Noted. I'll loop in infra for CDN redirect rules and see if we can add a 301 pattern that preserves fragments where the source has them.

Liam O'Connor: Merged and cherry-picked to stable branch. Closing thread. :white_check_mark:
